.TH BLKCHECK 8 "November 2026" "nano-blk 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
blkcheck \- model-based data-integrity check for a block device
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B blkcheck
.I device ops seed
.RI [ maxlen_kb ]
.br
.B blkcheck
.I device
.B fill
.I seed
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B blkcheck
issues
.I ops
random 4 KiB-aligned O_DIRECT writes, reads and discards against
.I device
and compares every read with an in-memory copy of what the device must
contain.  It finishes with a read-back of the whole device and prints a
one-line JSON summary.
.PP
In
.B fill
mode it writes every 4 KiB block once, in order, continuing past failed
writes, then checks that written blocks read back exactly and that blocks
whose write failed read back as zeroes.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if every read matched the model; 1 on any mismatch or I/O error.
.SH WARNING
All data on
.I device
is overwritten.
